# CI and pull-request verification

Repository: `setnessconsulting/game-ai-playtest-lab`
Risk tier: `LOW` in the live `project-jenkins-config` policy.
Routine PR workflow: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (GitHub Actions, same-repository PRs only)
Current required PR checks: none in live `main` protection; re-read protection for every PR.
Jenkins catalog profile: `game-ai-playtest-lab-python312` (`qualified`; qualification evidence does not establish a merge gate)
Owner-controlled Actions fallback: `.github/workflows/jenkins-fallback.yml` (manual `workflow_dispatch`, exact-SHA)
Fork PR support: `not qualified`
Deployment boundary: verification does not deploy; release and deployment remain outside CI.

- Before reviewing a pull request, refresh its head SHA, live check results and sources, required checks, and unresolved review threads.
- LOW-risk pull requests use GitHub Actions only for routine PR verification. The `ci.yml` workflow skips build and test work for documentation-only changes and rejects fork pull requests before checkout.
- The Jenkins profile records prior qualification evidence but is not a routine PR lane under the LOW policy. Jenkins remains separate for comprehensive, owner-triggered E2E when a current approved route exists.
- `.github/workflows/jenkins-fallback.yml` remains an owner-controlled manual exact-SHA Actions fallback; do not dispatch Jenkins or Actions as routine PR verification.
- Never run a pull-request-supplied Jenkinsfile or expose the GitHub App private key, Checks-write credential, production secret, controller data, Docker socket, or persistent agent state to repository code.
- Fork verification stays disabled until the per-run untrusted sandbox is qualified. A maintainer-applied `jenkins-verify` label is opt-in only and never substitutes for isolation.
- Keep CI separate from release/deployment. Do not deploy or change deployment configuration as part of verification.
- In review summaries, include the exact head SHA, authoritative required checks and results, Jenkins status when applicable, residual Actions coverage, and unresolved verification limits.
